NAME
       nfsstat - show NFS statistics

SYNOPSIS
       nfsstat [-c] [-s] [-m]

DESCRIPTION
       nfsstat prints counters kept by the kernel's NFS client and server:
       how many remote procedure calls were made, how many were retried, and
       per operation. A rising retrans count points to network or server
       trouble.

OPTIONS
       -c     Client statistics only.

       -s     Server statistics only.

       -m     List the NFS mounts with their options (version, timeouts).

EXAMPLES
           nfsstat -c
           nfsstat -m

SEE ALSO
       mount.nfs(8), showmount(8)
